ledger_metrics.subject_align_prompt:
Below are two lists of names used in this system. The first list is the names the policy constants are recorded under. The second list is the names as they appear in this customer's own records.

Names in the policy constants:
{subjects}

Names in the customer's records:
{groups}

For each name in the second list, say which name in the first list refers to the same thing. Copy both names exactly as written. Reply with a JSON object only, mapping each name from the second list to the name from the first list it refers to. Leave out any name you are not sure about - do not guess, and do not invent names that are not in the lists. If none of them refer to the same thing, reply {{}}.

ledger_metrics.case_facts_prompt:
Report the following, and nothing else:

{items}

Report a number ONLY if the conversation below actually states it. Values are integers, digits only, no currency symbol or separators. If the conversation gives a range or an approximation, use the number it states. Omit any item the conversation does not state - do not infer it, do not estimate it, and do not use general knowledge. Every item you report needs a quote copied exactly from the conversation. If none are stated, reply {{}}. Reply with the JSON object only.

Conversation:
{text}

ledger_metrics.rederive_prompt:
{table}

What is on record for this customer:
{facts}

The customer says:
{asked}

Answer with one name copied exactly from the list above, and nothing else. If the customer's words do not single out one, reply NONE.

ledger_metrics.decided_text:
A separate check was run on the policy constants on record, with this customer's situation and nothing else from this conversation in front of it. It answers: {choice}.
The figures it used: {operands}
The row it settled on: {row}
The next best ones it ranked, in order: {runners}

ledger_metrics.objective_axis_prompt:
The customer is asking for something to be maximised. Here are the quantities on record:
{axes}

Conversation:
{text}

Which ONE of the names listed above is the quantity the customer wants to be as large as possible? Reply with that name exactly as written and nothing else. If the conversation does not single one out, reply NONE.

ledger_metrics.objective_axes_prompt:
The customer is asking for something to be maximised, and it may be a total of more than one of the quantities on record. Here are the quantities on record:
{axes}

Conversation:
{text}

Which of the names listed above make up the quantity the customer wants to be as large as possible? If the customer wants two or more of them added together, name each one. Reply with the name or names exactly as written, one per line, and nothing else. If the conversation does not single any out, reply NONE.

